.TH SDL_GUID 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_GUID \- An
.BR SDL_GUID
is a 128-bit identifier for an input device that identifies that device across runs of SDL programs on the same platform.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_guid.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef struct SDL_GUID {
.BI "    Uint8 data[16];
.BI "} SDL_GUID;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If the device is detached and then re-attached to a different port, or if the base system is rebooted, the device should still report the same GUID\[char46]
.PP
GUIDs are as precise as possible but are not guaranteed to distinguish physically distinct but equivalent devices\[char46] For example, two game controllers from the same vendor with the same product ID and revision may have the same GUID\[char46]
.PP
GUIDs may be platform-dependent (i\[char46]e\[char46], the same device may report different GUIDs on different operating systems)\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This struct is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

